# UX Specification: EnviroFlow Visual Automation

**Source PRD:** `visual-automation-prd.md`
**Autonomy Level:** L5 - Execute (with L4 decision logic)
**Primary Data Sources:** Supabase (workflows, activity_logs, controllers), AC Infinity Cloud API (live sensors + device control), MQTT brokers (cross-manufacturer sensors)

---

## Pass 1: Mental Model

**Autonomy level:** L5 - Execute
**User role at this level:** Supervisor — monitors autonomous execution, intervenes when needed

**Primary user intent:** "I want my grow environment to automatically respond to conditions without me constantly checking, but I need to stay in control and understand what's happening."

**Existing mental model (from current tools):**

| Tool | What Users Expect | How EnviroFlow Differs |
|------|-------------------|----------------------|
| AC Infinity App | Per-device modes (AUTO, VPD, TIMER). Simple threshold → action. | EnviroFlow adds cross-device logic, delays, variables, multi-step flows |
| Home Assistant | When/And/Then automations. Device state visibility. | Similar structure but visual canvas instead of YAML, simpler setup |
| Node-RED | Drag-and-drop nodes, wires, debug/trace. | Same paradigm, but domain-specific nodes (Sensor, Dimmer, Mode) |
| Spreadsheets | IF(temp > 82, "fan on", "fan off"). Predictable. | Same logic, but automated execution instead of reference |

**Likely misconceptions:**

1. **"Real-time execution"** — Users expect instant response when sensor crosses threshold. Reality: 1-minute cron cycle means up to 60-second delay.
   - *Mitigation:* Show "Checks every 60 seconds" in trigger node. First-time tooltip on activation.

2. **"Unlimited commands"** — Users may create many sensor-triggered workflows. Reality: ~30 commands/min per user, ~60 reads/min per AC Infinity account.
   - *Mitigation:* Rate limit indicator when approaching limits. Warning during workflow activation if combined active workflows could exceed.

3. **"Workflows are independent"** — Users won't realize two workflows targeting the same port conflict. Reality: Conflicting workflows block each other.
   - *Mitigation:* Pre-activation conflict check. Red "Conflict" badge. Clear resolution flow.

4. **"Delay pauses everything"** — Users may think a delay node stops all workflows. Reality: Only that workflow's execution path pauses; others continue.
   - *Mitigation:* Delay node tooltip: "This workflow waits here. Other workflows continue normally."

5. **"The sensor value is live"** — Users see a number in the properties panel and assume it's real-time. Reality: Sensors update every 15 seconds via polling.
   - *Mitigation:* Show "as of X seconds ago" next to sensor values.

6. **"EnviroFlow replaces AC Infinity modes"** — Users may think workflows override AC Infinity native programming. Reality: Both can run simultaneously, potentially conflicting.
   - *Mitigation:* Show current AC Infinity mode on device nodes. Warn if workflow targets a port with an active native mode.

**Autonomy-specific concerns:**

| Concern | User Thinking | UX Response |
|---------|---------------|-------------|
| Trust | "How do I know it ran?" | Activity log with timestamps, execution trace |
| Control | "What if it goes wrong at 2am?" | Push notifications on failure, emergency pause |
| Predictability | "What will this workflow do?" | Dry-run/test button, execution preview |
| Accountability | "Why did my fan turn off?" | Execution history showing which node, which sensor value, which rule |
| Intervention | "I need to stop this NOW" | Pause workflow button, always accessible |
| Coexistence | "Will this fight with my AC Infinity settings?" | Native mode visibility, conflict warnings |

**UX principle to reinforce:** The system executes autonomously within user-defined boundaries. Users are supervisors, not operators. Every autonomous action must be: (1) visible after the fact, (2) explainable with specific data, (3) stoppable at the workflow level.

---

## Pass 2: Information Architecture

**All user-visible concepts:**

| Concept | Category | Data Source | Refresh Rate |
|---------|----------|-------------|--------------|
| Workflow definition | Entity | Supabase `workflows` | On save/load |
| Workflow status | Status | Supabase `workflows.is_active` + conflict check | On load + mutation |
| Node configuration | Entity | Supabase `workflows.nodes` JSONB | On save/load |
| Edge connections | Entity | Supabase `workflows.edges` JSONB | On save/load |
| Controller list | Entity | Supabase `controllers` | On page load |
| Controller ports | Entity | `/api/controllers/[id]/capabilities` | On page load + 5-min cache |
| Port current state (ON/OFF, level) | Metric | AC Infinity API via capabilities | On load + 30s polling |
| Native AC Infinity mode | Metric | AC Infinity API via `/api/controllers/[id]/modes` | On load + 30s polling |
| Live sensor readings | Metric | AC Infinity API via `/api/sensors/live` | 15s polling |
| Execution history | Log | Supabase `activity_logs` | On demand + after execution |
| Delay countdown | Metric | Calculated from `resume_after` timestamp | Every second (client-side) |
| Rate limit usage | Metric | In-memory rate limiter | Real-time (per request) |
| Workflow conflicts | Alert | Calculated from active workflow port targets | On workflow activation |
| Templates (built-in) | Entity | Static JSON bundled with app | Static |
| Templates (personal) | Entity | Supabase (future) | On demand |
| MQTT broker connection | Status | MQTT adapter | 🔄 Planned — On connect + heartbeat |
| MQTT topic subscriptions | Entity | Workflow config | 🔄 Planned — On save/load |
| Hysteresis state | Status | Runtime execution state | Per execution cycle |
| Debounce cooldown | Status | Runtime execution state | Per execution cycle |
| Variable values | Metric | Supabase `workflow_variables` | On read/write |

**Grouped structure:**

### Node Palette (workflow builder left sidebar)

| Concept | Visibility | Rationale |
|---------|------------|-----------|
| **Triggers** (Schedule, Sensor, Manual) | Primary — always visible | Entry point for all workflows |
| **Sensors** (Sensor node) | Primary — always visible | Most common condition source |
| **Logic** (Condition AND/OR) | Primary — always visible | Core building blocks |
| **Actions** (Device Control, Dimmer) | Primary — always visible | Main output mechanism |
| **Flow Control** (Delay, Debounce) | Secondary — expandable section | Advanced users; not every workflow needs these |
| **Variables** (Variable node) | Secondary — expandable section | Power users building stateful workflows |
| **Device Programming** (Mode, Verified Action, Port Condition) | Secondary — expandable section | Power user / AC Infinity-specific features |
| **Notifications** (Notification node) | Secondary — expandable section | Not every workflow sends alerts |

### Device Tree (within Node Palette)

| Concept | Visibility | Rationale |
|---------|------------|-----------|
| Controller name + online/offline indicator | Primary | Must know status before dragging |
| Port list (nested under controller) | Primary | What users actually drag to canvas |
| Port device type icon + name | Primary | Quick identification |
| Port current state [ON 80%] / [OFF] | Primary | Context for workflow building |
| Built-in sensor (Temp/Humidity/VPD) | Primary | Common trigger source |
| Controller offline = dimmed, not draggable | Primary | Prevents building flows against unreachable devices |
| **Native AC Infinity mode badge on action nodes** | Read-only | Shows current native programming; editable only on Controllers page (not canvas) |

### Canvas (workflow builder center)

| Concept | Visibility | Rationale |
|---------|------------|-----------|
| Placed nodes with type-specific styling | Primary | Core editing surface |
| Edge connections between nodes | Primary | Defines flow |
| Node selection highlight | Primary | Shows what's being edited |
| Snap-to-grid (16px) | Hidden (automatic behavior) | Clean alignment without user effort |
| Zoom controls + mini-map | Secondary (corner controls) | Large workflow navigation |

### Properties Panel (workflow builder right sidebar)

| Concept | Visibility | Rationale |
|---------|------------|-----------|
| Selected node's configuration form | Primary | Main editing surface for node settings |
| Sensor threshold + operator | Primary | Core condition config |
| Hysteresis settings (trigger + re-arm) | Primary (when sensor node selected) | Prevents flapping — must be easy to configure |
| **Variable node config** | Primary (when variable node selected) | See Variable Node UX below |
| Live sensor reading | Secondary (below config) | Debugging aid, not primary input |
| "Last updated X seconds ago" | Secondary (inline) | Builds trust in sensor data |

### Variable Node UX Design

**Canvas Display:**
- **Header:** Variable name (user-defined, e.g., "spray_count")
- **Body:** Operation icon + scope badge
  - Set: `=` icon + value
  - Get: `→` icon + "reads value"
  - Increment: `+` icon + amount
  - Decrement: `-` icon + amount
- **Scope badge:** Workflow (blue) or Global (purple)

**Properties Panel Form:**

| Field | Type | Options/Validation |
|-------|------|--------------------|
| Variable Name | Text input | Required. `[a-z_][a-z0-9_]*` pattern. Auto-suggest existing names. |
| Scope | Radio | **Workflow** (default, isolated to this workflow) or **Global** (shared across workflows) |
| Operation | Dropdown | Set, Get, Increment, Decrement |
| Value Type | Dropdown (for Set) | Number, String, Boolean |
| Value | Dynamic input | Number input, text input, or toggle based on type |
| Amount | Number input (for Inc/Dec) | Default: 1 |

**Scope Explanation (inline help):**
- **Workflow scope:** "This variable exists only during this workflow run. Resets each execution."
- **Global scope:** "This variable persists between runs and can be read by other workflows."

**Canvas States:**
- **Configured:** Shows `var_name = 5` or `var_name += 1`
- **Unconfigured:** Orange warning, "Set variable name"
- **In execution trace:** Shows actual value: `spray_count was 3 → now 4`

### Activity Panel (workflow builder bottom or tab)

| Concept | Visibility | Rationale |
|---------|------------|-----------|
| Recent execution entries | Primary | Trust-building — "yes, it's working" |
| Execution status (success/failed/skipped) | Primary | Quick health check |
| Timestamp | Primary | Recency context |
| Execution node trace (expandable) | Secondary | Debugging — which nodes ran, with what values |
| Error messages | Primary (when error exists) | Requires immediate attention |

### Controllers Page (native mode display)

| Concept | Visibility | Rationale |
|---------|------------|-----------|
| Mode badge (AUTO/VPD/TIMER/CYCLE/SCHEDULE) | Primary | Quick identification of current programming |
| Mode-specific summary | Primary | "75-85°F, 50-65% RH" at a glance |
| "Program Mode" action | Secondary (menu item) | Not frequent; available when needed |
| Color-coded mode badges | Primary | Visual differentiation: AUTO=Blue, VPD=Purple, TIMER=Amber, CYCLE=Cyan, SCHEDULE=Green |

### Mode Programming Panel Design

**Location:** Slide-over panel from right edge, triggered by "Program Mode" action on port card.

**Structure:**
1. **Mode Selector** (top): Radio buttons for OFF / ON / AUTO / VPD / TIMER / CYCLE / SCHEDULE
2. **Mode-specific form** (middle): Fields change based on selected mode
3. **Actions** (bottom): Cancel / Apply Mode button

**Per-Mode Form Fields:**

| Mode | Fields | Validation |
|------|--------|------------|
| OFF | None | — |
| ON | Level slider (0-10) | Required |
| AUTO | Trigger High (°F), Trigger Low (°F), Device Behavior (dropdown) | High > Low |
| VPD | VPD High (kPa), VPD Low (kPa), Leaf Temp Offset (°F) | High > Low, 0.4–1.8 range warning |
| TIMER | Timer Type (On/Off), Duration (minutes) | Duration 1–720 |
| CYCLE | On Duration (min), Off Duration (min) | Both > 0 |
| SCHEDULE | Start Time (HH:MM), End Time (HH:MM), Days (checkboxes) | Valid times |

**Common Fields (all modes except OFF):**
- Min Level (0-10)
- Max Level (0-10)
- Transition Speed (slow/medium/fast) — shown only if device supports dimming
- Buffer Enabled (toggle) + Buffer Value (°F/%)

**Validation UX:**
- Inline validation on blur
- Red border + error message below field
- Apply button disabled until all errors resolved
- Pre-fill with current device values on open

### Template Gallery

| Concept | Visibility | Rationale |
|---------|------------|-----------|
| Template name + description | Primary | What this template does |
| Template preview (node graph) | Primary | Visual understanding before applying |
| "Built-in" vs "Personal" filter | Primary | Two distinct sources |
| Device mapping requirements | Secondary (shown on select) | What devices the template needs |

**Template Application Flow (PRD Section 10.3):**

| Step | Screen | User Action | System Response |
|------|--------|-------------|-----------------|
| 1. Browse | Template Gallery modal | Browse/search templates | Display template cards with name, description, category |
| 2. Preview | Template detail view | Click "Use Template" on card | Show full template preview: node graph, device requirements, description |
| 3. Map Devices | Device Mapping Wizard | Select user devices for each template requirement | Auto-match by type+room, show "3 of 4 matched", dropdowns for manual override |
| 4. Create Draft | — | Click "Create Workflow" | Create inactive draft workflow with mapped devices, navigate to builder |

**Wizard Step Details:**

- **Step 2 - Preview:** Shows read-only node canvas, lists "Requires: 1 exhaust fan, 1 VPD sensor", "Use Template" button proceeds to Step 3
- **Step 3 - Map Devices:** Table format, validation blocks proceed until all devices mapped, "Back" returns to preview
- **Step 4 - Result:** Toast "Workflow created from template", redirects to `/automations/builder/[new-id]` with workflow in draft state

**Cross-source relationships:**

| Relationship | Sources Involved | Conflict Potential |
|--------------|------------------|-------------------|
| Sensor threshold vs live reading | AC Infinity API + Workflow config | Low — display only |
| Port state vs action target | AC Infinity API + Action node config | Medium — stale state possible (30s lag) |
| Multiple workflows → same port | Supabase workflows (computed) | High — explicit conflict detection required |
| Native AC Infinity mode vs workflow action | AC Infinity API + Workflow config | High — both can control the same port |
| Template devices vs user devices | Template JSON + User's controllers | High — mapping wizard required |
| MQTT topic vs sensor type | MQTT broker + Workflow config | Low — user explicitly maps |

**Data provenance decisions:**

- **Show source label:** Sensor readings (AC Infinity badge), MQTT sensors (MQTT badge)
- **Show last-updated timestamp:** All sensor readings in properties panel, execution log entries
- **Show confidence/state indicator:** Hysteresis state ("Triggered"/"Re-armed" badge), Debounce state ("Cooling down"/"Ready")

---

## Pass 3: Affordances

### User Actions

| Action | Consequence Level | Visual/Interaction Signal |
|--------|-------------------|---------------------------|
| Drag node from palette to canvas | Safe | Drag cursor, drop preview shadow, snap to grid |
| Drag port from device tree to canvas | Safe | Same as above; creates pre-configured action/sensor node |
| Connect nodes with edge | Safe | Draggable handle, animated connection preview, snap to valid targets |
| Edit node properties | Safe | Form inputs in properties panel, changes saved on blur/enter |
| Delete node (draft workflow) | Safe | X button on hover, no confirmation needed |
| Delete node (active workflow) | Consequential | X button + warning "This workflow is active" |
| Save workflow | Safe | Standard button, toast confirmation |
| Name/rename workflow | Safe | Inline text field |
| Duplicate workflow | Safe | Creates new draft copy with " (Copy)" suffix |
| **Activate workflow** | **Consequential** | Toggle switch → green "Active" state. Pre-activation checks: conflict scan, validation. Toast: "Workflow activated — checking every 60 seconds" |
| Pause workflow | Safe | Toggle switch → yellow "Paused" state. Immediate stop of execution. |
| **Manual trigger ("Run Now")** | **Consequential** | Distinct button (not the toggle). Shows "Running..." then result toast. |
| **Delete workflow** | **Destructive** | Menu item (not primary button). Confirmation modal with workflow name. |
| Pause active delay | Consequential | Pause icon on delay node countdown. Extends wait indefinitely until resumed. |
| **Resolve conflict** | **Consequential** | Modal with side-by-side comparison. Choose which workflow keeps Active. |
| Export workflow as JSON | Safe | Download button, instant download |
| Import workflow from JSON | Safe (creates draft) | File picker → validation → creates inactive draft |
| Apply template | Consequential | Multi-step wizard: preview → device mapping → create draft |
| **Save as Template** | Safe | Menu item in workflow builder. Modal to name + describe template. Saves to personal templates. |
| **Program AC Infinity mode** | **Consequential** | Opens mode config panel. Changes sent to AC Infinity API immediately. Confirmation toast with undo (5s window). |

### System Actions (L5 autonomy visibility)

| System Action | User Visibility | Override Affordance |
|---------------|-----------------|---------------------|
| Cron evaluates workflow | Activity log entry with timestamp | Pause workflow to prevent future evaluations |
| Sensor threshold crossed | Sensor node shows "Triggered" badge in execution trace | Wait for hysteresis re-arm, or pause workflow |
| Command sent to device | Activity log: "Set Port 1 to Speed 8" with timestamp | No undo (committed). Can send counter-command manually. |
| Delay countdown started | Timer on delay node: "Resuming in 4:32" | Click to pause or cancel delay |
| Rate limit hit | Toast: "Commands queued" + indicator with queue count | Wait for reset (shows countdown) |
| Workflow blocked by conflict | Red "Conflict" badge + notification | Resolve via conflict modal |
| Verified action failed | Activity log with failure + auto-rollback note | Automatic rollback if configured; manual retry available |
| Execution halted mid-flow | Push notification + "Failed" badge | View error, edit workflow, manual retry |
| Debounce cooldown active | "Cooling down" indicator on debounce node | Wait for cooldown to expire |

**Affordance rules:**

1. **Green "Active" badge** → workflow executes automatically on cron
2. **Yellow "Paused" badge** → workflow will not execute
3. **Red "Conflict" badge** → both conflicting workflows are blocked from executing
4. **System-initiated actions** use a clock/cron icon; **user-initiated actions** show user context
5. **Consequential actions** (activate, manual trigger, program mode) require single click + clear visual feedback (not a modal, but a distinct state change)
6. **Destructive actions** (delete) require explicit confirmation with the workflow name typed or displayed

**Reversibility signals:**

| State | Reversible? | Signal |
|-------|-------------|--------|
| Draft workflow (unsaved) | Yes | "Unsaved changes" dot indicator |
| Saved workflow (inactive) | Yes | Can edit freely, no consequences |
| Active workflow | Partial | Can pause to edit; changes take effect on next cron cycle |
| Command sent to device | No | "Sent at HH:MM" in log. No undo button. Can send counter-command. |
| Delay in progress | Yes | Pause/cancel button on delay node |
| AC Infinity mode programmed | Partial | 5-second undo toast after mode change |
| Conflict blocking | Yes | Resolve by choosing which workflow to keep active |

---

## Pass 4: Cognitive Load

**Volume context:**
- Expected: 10-50 workflows per user, 5-20 active simultaneously
- Each workflow: 3-10 nodes typically
- Executions: potentially hundreds/day with many sensor triggers
- AC Infinity modes: 5 mode types × N ports to potentially configure

**Friction points:**

| Moment | Type | Location | Simplification |
|--------|------|----------|----------------|
| Choosing which node type | Choice | Node palette | Category grouping with icons. Tooltip descriptions on hover. Search box for 12+ nodes. |
| Configuring sensor threshold | Choice | Properties panel | Show current reading next to threshold input. Suggest common values based on sensor type. |
| Understanding hysteresis vs debounce | Uncertainty | Sensor/Debounce node config | Inline help with use-case examples (see Hysteresis vs Debounce Guidance below) |
| Configuring hysteresis band | Uncertainty | Sensor node properties | Visual mini-diagram showing trigger zone and re-arm zone with current reading marker |
| MQTT topic syntax | Uncertainty | MQTT trigger config | Input with examples: "home/sensor/#", validation on blur, "Test Connection" button |
| JSONPath payload conditions | Uncertainty | MQTT trigger config | Example payloads from last received message, visual JSONPath builder |
| Mapping template devices | Choice | Template wizard | Smart auto-match by device type + room, show "3 of 4 matched" confidence, manual override for unmatched |
| AC Infinity mode programming | Choice | Mode config panel | Pre-fill with current values. Group by mode type. Show what each setting does. |
| Trusting workflow execution | Trust | Before/after activation | "Test Run" button (below Save, secondary style). Opens modal with: (1) mock sensor inputs with sliders, (2) "Simulate" button, (3) trace preview showing which nodes would fire + what commands would send. No actual API calls. |
| Understanding rate limits | Uncertainty | During heavy usage | Proactive warning at 70% capacity. Show "24/30 commands used, resets in 45s" |
| Debugging why workflow didn't fire | Uncertainty | After expected execution | Activity log shows "Skipped: temperature 78°F below threshold 82°F" |
| Many workflows, which ones matter? | Volume | Workflow list | Filter by: Active/Paused/Failed. Sort by: Last run, Name, Room. Search. |
| Resolving conflicts | Choice | Conflict alert | Side-by-side comparison of conflicting workflows. Clear "Keep this one" / "Keep other" buttons. |
| Delay node + cron interaction | Uncertainty | During delay | Help text: "Workflow pauses here. Resumes on the first cron cycle after the timer completes (~60s precision)." |

**Defaults introduced:**

| Default | Rationale | Override Visibility |
|---------|-----------|---------------------|
| Hysteresis enabled (5-unit band below trigger) | Prevents flapping; most sensor triggers need this | Toggle + custom value in sensor node properties |
| Delay unit = minutes | Most delays are 1-30 minutes | Dropdown selector: seconds, minutes, hours |
| Debounce cooldown = 60 seconds | Reasonable default for most triggers | Number input in debounce node |
| Notification channel = push | Universally available | Multi-select: push, email, SMS |
| Verified action retries = 3 | Balances reliability and speed | Number input |
| Workflow starts as Draft (inactive) | Prevents accidental autonomous execution | Must explicitly toggle Active |
| Template auto-match by type + room | Reduces manual mapping effort | Manual override available for each device |

### Hysteresis vs Debounce Guidance

**Inline Help Content (displayed in properties panel):**

**Hysteresis** — *"Wait until value drops below X before allowing re-trigger"*
| When to use | Example |
|-------------|----------|
| Sensor oscillates near threshold | Temp hits 82°F, fan starts. Temp drops to 81°F, fan stops. Temp hits 82°F again. **Without hysteresis:** Fan cycles every few seconds. **With hysteresis (re-arm at 77°F):** Fan stays on until temp drops to 77°F. |
| Prevent device wear | Exhaust fan, humidifier, or any device that shouldn't cycle rapidly. |
| **Summary:** | Use when you want the *value* to return to a safe zone before re-triggering. |

**Debounce** — *"Wait N seconds before allowing another trigger, regardless of value"*
| When to use | Example |
|-------------|----------|
| Intentional cooldown period | After emergency fan activation, wait 5 minutes before allowing another emergency trigger. |
| Rate-limit expensive actions | Notifications, API calls, or actions with real-world cost. |
| **Summary:** | Use when you want *time* to pass before re-triggering, regardless of sensor value. |

**Decision Flow:**
1. Is the issue that the sensor hovers near the threshold? → Use **Hysteresis**
2. Is the issue that you need a cooldown period after action? → Use **Debounce**
3. Need both? Chain them: Trigger → Debounce → Action (debounce protects action frequency, hysteresis on trigger prevents evaluation flapping)

### Cross-Controller Unlock UX (F10 Value Prop)

**Onboarding Tooltip (first time adding MQTT sensor):**
> "🌟 **Unlock Cross-Manufacturer Control**
> You can now trigger AC Infinity devices from *any* sensor — Inkbird, Ecowitt, Govee, or any MQTT-compatible device.
> 
> **Example:** Use your Inkbird soil moisture sensor to trigger your AC Infinity humidifier."

**Tooltip on MQTT Trigger Node:**
> "Connect external sensors via MQTT to control AC Infinity devices. This is what makes EnviroFlow unique."

**Template Gallery Badge:**
- Templates using MQTT sensors show "🔗 Cross-Controller" badge
- Tooltip: "This template uses sensors from one brand to control devices from another."

**Batch handling strategy:**

- **Review individually:** New workflow creation, conflict resolution, mode programming
- **Review by exception:** Active workflows list (filter to "Failed" or "Blocked" status)
- **Auto-process:** Template device mapping (auto-matched devices don't need review)

**Trust-building elements:**

| System Action | Trust Signal |
|---------------|--------------|
| Sensor threshold evaluation | "Current: 78°F. Threshold: 82°F. Status: Below threshold." |
| Hysteresis state | Mini-diagram: "Trigger at 82°F ▲ / Re-arm at 77°F ▼. Currently: re-armed." |
| Workflow execution | Activity log: "12:34:05 — Sensor checked: 84°F > 82°F → Triggered → Set Fan Speed 8 → Success" |
| Template device matching | "3 of 4 devices auto-matched (by type + room). 1 needs manual selection." |
| Delay countdown | Live timer: "Resuming in 4:32 (~12:38 PM)" |
| Rate limit status | "24/30 commands used this minute. Resets in 45s." |
| Dry-run result | "Test complete: Would set Port 1 to Speed 8 (not actually sent)" |

